<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Australia's Hambro-Grantham boosts capital.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Australia's Hambro-Grantham boosts capital.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian fund manager Hambro-Grantham said on Wednesday that on completion of its new A$75 million Hambro-Grantham Fund 5, the group would have A$200 million of funds under management.</p>
<p>Hambro-Grantham said the new fund would target 15 to 25 growth oriented businesses established for at three years with revenues of between A$5 million and A$100 million and projected growth of at least 20 percent per annum.</p>
<p>It said the information technology/communications sector, which accounted for 36 percent of the group's investments to date, would continue to be a focus for new investment.</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
